WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.170
- [Instructor] So in this video,

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:03.240
we're going to think
about dividing numbers

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:06.480
where the quotient, the
result of our division,

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.000
might result in a decimal.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.390
So let's say we wanted to compute

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:13.370
what five divided by two is.

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:14.590
In the past, you might've said,

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:16.470
hey, two times two is four

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:18.110
and then you'd have one leftover

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:20.040
and so you might have
said something like this,

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.420
this is two with a remainder of one.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:24.940
But now we don't want,
we don't wanna just say,

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:27.420
hey, how many times can it
go in and what's left over.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:31.260
We wanna know exactly how many
times can two go into five

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.780
so we want a decimal
answer right over here.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.580
So, pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.070
All right, now let's work
through this together.

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:42.150
And there's many ways that
we could approach this.

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:45.160
One way is to realize
that five divided by two,

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:48.480
we could re-express as five divided by two

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.160
or as five halves and five
halves is the same thing

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:56.930
as four plus one over two

00:00:56.930 --> 00:01:01.660
which is the same thing as
four halves plus one half

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:04.760
which is the same thing
as four halves is two.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.190
Let me do that in a different color.

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:07.840
This part over here is two

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.290
and then you have this one half.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:11.950
So it's the same thing as two and a half

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:14.600
and if we were to
express that as a decimal

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:17.020
that's going to be equal to two

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:20.950
and how many tenths is equal to a half?

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:24.140
Well five tenths is equal to a half.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.290
So five divided by two,
you could say, 2.5.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:30.540
Now another way that you could
approach this is you say,

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:34.070
five divided by two is the same thing as

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:36.420
50 tenths divided by two.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.040
So let me use a different color here.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:40.390
So instead of a five, I could say five

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:43.410
is the same thing as 50 tenths,

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:46.110
50 tenths divided by,

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:47.710
divided by two

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:49.960
and so if I have 50 of something

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:52.280
and if I were to divide it by two,

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:55.350
well that's going to result
in 25 of the something.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:59.730
So this is going to be equal to 25 tenths.

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:03.920
And how would we express
25 tenths as a decimal?

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.780
Well, this is going to be equal to,

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:08.810
if I could put some place values here,

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:11.400
so we definitely have five tenths.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.060
I'll put that in the tenths place

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:18.060
and then 20 tenths is the
same thing as two ones.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:20.160
And that's exactly what we had up here.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.580
Either way, you get 2.5,

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:23.153
two ones and five tenths.

